  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Existence of a CPG development effectiveness strategy / partnership framework
Existence of inclusive national annual/biennial policy dialogue that reviews progress on development finance and cooperation and externally financed development projects/programmes</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2018">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) CPG awareness raising information note
(2) Eleven policy meeting summary notes
(3) Six briefing /analysis pieces informing meetings/policy dialogue 
(4) One Coordination Structure finalized</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) A CPG project extension proposal for 2020-2022 was developed through consultation with the CPG members and finalized in August 2020. The project extension proposal reflected on the strategic priorities drawn from previous discussions and has revised the strategy and outputs for the next two years with a view to contributing to a broader exchange among Cooperation Partners (CPs) and with other key stakeholders (Government, EAOs, INGOs, CSOs). 

(2) Eleven monthly policy meetings with the Facilitators and Alternates of the CPG were held and eleven summary notes produced. The meetings provided opportunities to discuss issues of importance or urgency that needs to be dealt with through the CPG, either through Work Streams or through dedicated meetings as well as providing a space to discuss short- and mid-term COVID relief and recovery efforts which will inform CPG members&#x2019; work. 

(3) Six briefing /analysis pieces informing meetings/policy dialogue were prepared. These includes briefing /analysis documents for (a) two DACU-CPG meetings (in May and August); (b) CPG collective input to the Development Assistance Policy (DAP); (c) CPG collective input to the draft Myanmar Economic Recovery and Reform Plan (MERRP); (d) mapping of CPG engagement with the Sector Coordination Group (SCG); (e) Strategic Coordination Group Restructuring Matrix. 

(4) The new, government-led Strategic Coordination Groups were finalized in November 2020 in full consultation with the CPG. The Secretariat documented the restructuring process and supported key discussions which will inform CPG members&#x2019; participation in the new coordination structure.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1)	Number of dedicated meetings between CPG and Government actors in support of national development priorities and SDGs (the number was never decided upon)

2)	Existence of inclusive national annual/biennial policy dialogue that review progress on development finance and cooperation and externally financed development projects/programmes</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1)	Due to the changing context in Myanmar, there was no opportunity to organize a dedicated meeting between CPG and the Government actors in support of national development priorities and SDGs.

2)	The new, government-led Strategic Coordination Groups were finalized in November 2020 in full consultation with the CPG. The Secretariat documented the restructuring process and supported key discussions which would inform CPG members&#x2019; participation in the new coordination structure for 2021. However, while in the process of scheduling the first dialogues for 2021, the February event overtook the planning. Currently, some of the strategic coordination, including development finance, is taken forward by UN agencies and bilateral members, but without de facto authorities or any government representative.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1)	Number of dedicated meetings between CPG and Government actors in support of national development priorities and SDGs (the number was never decided upon)

2)	Existence of inclusive national annual/biennial policy dialogue that review progress on development finance and cooperation and externally financed development projects/programmes</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
